comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:14:18.504Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: exact advisory-id searches across all pm statuses returned zero items. Broader package searches found only closed predecessor advisories pm-5q81jq, pm-f5hy2n, and pm-a24aqt for different GHSAs; this item preserves new advisory lineage instead of reopening completed fixes."
  "2026-08-03T18:40:17.025Z","harness:codex","Security evidence: pnpm audit initially reported high GHSA-rgw5-rvv9-x895 through brace-expansion 5.0.8 and moderate GHSA-fxqj-rqcc-2cmp through postcss 8.5.22 while GitHub Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning APIs each reported zero open alerts. Overrides now require brace-expansion >=5.0.9 <6 and postcss >=8.5.23 <9; the resolved graph uses patched versions and pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities. tsx was refreshed to 4.23.5."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:40:17.470Z","harness:codex","Compatibility boundary: npm-package-arg 14 is intentionally deferred because its Node engine excludes the supported Node 22.18 floor. TypeScript 7 is intentionally deferred because typescript-eslint 8.66 supports TypeScript below 6.1. These are incompatible majors rather than unattended safe updates."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:40:17.932Z","harness:codex",GitHub alert APIs can be clean while a newly published advisory is already visible to the package-manager audit. Release readiness needs both remote alert inventories and a fresh lockfile-native audit with explicit secure override floors.
